ing all new yorkers and all bronx  sites to please join us in praying for  these families no one expected to wake  up on a sunday morning hearing about a  fire in their building running for their  lives this is profound sadness for all  of us but we know that in times of  challenge new yorkers step up because  that's just what we do and so we are  going to love on this community and love  on these residents and families and let  them know that they are not alone we  will walk this journey together to make  sure they have everything that is needed  i am grateful for the incredible support  from governor kathy hokel lieutenant  governor brian benjamin and all of my  colleagues in government we're going to  work together to make sure that we  prevent any tragedy from happening in  this magnitude ever again thank you so  much everyone i am so grateful and so  proud to be the borough president of a  borough like the bronx where we are  resilient we are tough and we are going  to turn our pain into purpose god bless  us all and thank you so much to all of  our first responders for your incredible  support  uh good afternoon i'm congressman richie  torres first i want to thank  the mayor who has been as visible and as  responsive and as compassionate and  comforting  as any leader as i've seen in a moment  of crisis the bronx is no stranger to  deadly fires i lived through one in  belmont just a few years ago  and so i'm enormously grateful to the  mayor to the city for mobilizing  resources  and in coming to our aid in a moment of  need you know the two things that are  most important to most of us  is our family and our homes and to lose  both in the span  of one tragedy  is terrifying and traumatic to an extent  that a few of us  could imagine what do you tell a mother  who's lost her children and who's lost  her home who's lost everything who's  seen  the world around her collapsed so we're  going to do our best to bring comfort to  those families  i do want to tell the mayor and the city  that  as a local congressman i'm committed to  advancing legislation  that addresses either the manufacturing  of space heaters or the need for  education about fire safety or the need  for self-closing doors and affordable  housing that receives federal funding so  you have a partner at the federal level  thank you  thank you so much everyone i'm  councilmember felice i represent uh this  area of the bronx  what happened yesterday was a  frightening nightmare  the bronx continues to have many  challenges and fire continues to be one  of them we've had some of the worst  fires in the city of new york right here  in the bronx including the belmont fire  including the one in woody crest  including the one yesterday where we  lost 19 lives including  babies four-year-olds  but i want to thank all of our wonderful  leaders our colleagues in government  cities  state and federal who have been here  around the clock and available and  providing all the resources needed to  all the affected families including food  including clothing and including housing  and as council member i'll be working  with my colleagues including our  congressman at the federal level our  borough president our mayor eric adams  and our state elected leaders  to make sure that we get additional  fire related laws to protect new yorkers  because we've had far too many fires and  this cannot continue to be the future of  our borough so we're going to be  continuing to work with our leaders to  make sure we strengthen some of our laws  analyze what exactly happened yesterday  and what we could learn from it and what  we can do to make sure it never happens  again thank you so much um for being  here thank you thank you i'm going to  bring on uh the uh the commissioner fire  commissioner uh nigro and  uh the deputy commissioner of oem for  there's any uh updates on what we're  doing and as we mobilize to move forward  thank you mayor the investigation  continues as i said yesterday were we're  certain that the fire started with a  faulty electrical  heater portable heater  the fire  was contained to the hallway just  outside this two-story apartment but the  smoke  traveled throughout the building and the  smoke is what caused the deaths and the  serious injuries  so our fire marshals teams are here  they've been here  they've been examining the building  they've been examining videotape they  will do a complete investigation as to  as to how this uh how this occurred why  this occurred and we're confident  of that as the mayor stated previously  uh patients were taken to seven  different hospitals there was a a bit of  a double count  and uh i guess it's a bit of good news  that the number isn't 19 but 17 but  don't forget there are many people  fighting for their lives in the hospital  who are transported so this number  could unfortunately uh increase again so  our prayers are with them and the  prayers  continue to be with the families of  those we lost  uh i will let oem discuss  more about the continued operations for  the families  thank you  uh so last night the building was  totally vacated uh no apartments were  habited last night we threw the american  red cross with housing preservation and  development and with the building  management about uh half of those units  so about 60 different families stayed in  area hotels we were able to house  everyone in the bronx  um and the rest as they said there are  people still in hospitals and people  also went to friends and family  ongoing is um  registration with the red cross people  are still people coming out of hospitals  people who are at work or somewhere else  so it's never too late people can  continue to register with the red cross  we worked with the department of  education they were able to help to get  the children back as was noted back to  their schools this morning  um and they will continue to help them  until people are back in the building uh  it does look like many o